# Feature Development Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)

When adding or modifying any layer primitive, engine domain capability, or MCP tool in MotionForge, you must execute the following sequential development checklist without skipping any step:

## 1. Schema Definition (`packages/scene-spec/`)
- Define the new layer or feature schema in `packages/scene-spec/src/layers/<kind>.ts` (or relevant domain schema file).
- Use `strictObject` and reuse shared primitives (`idSchema`, `msSchema`, `colorSchema`, `layerBaseSchema`).
- In `packages/scene-spec/src/scene.ts`:
  - Add the layer name to `LAYER_TYPES`.
  - Register the layer schema in `layerSchema` discriminated union.
  - Export inferred TypeScript types.

## 2. Sanitizer Normalization & Healing (`packages/scene-spec/src/sanitize.ts`)
- Add sanitization logic in `sanitizeSceneInput()` for the new schema.
- Normalize incoming raw values: clamp bounds, strip invalid transient keys (`_`-prefixed), ensure defaults for mandatory base attributes (`trackIndex`, `visible`, `locked`, `blendMode`).
- Ensure both engine (`EngineCore.saveScene`) and Studio (`services/engine-bridge.ts`) benefit from identical normalization.

## 3. Field Guide Documentation & Schema Examples (`packages/scene-spec/src/field-guide.ts`)
- Update `packages/scene-spec/src/field-guide.ts` to document the new primitive or capability.
- Provide:
  - Required and optional keys.
  - Nested shape contracts.
  - A fully schema-valid, copy-pasteable minimal example object.
- Ensure `tests/field-guide.spec.ts` passes so authoring guidance never drifts from schemas.

## 4. Deterministic Runtime Renderer (`packages/scene-runtime/`)
- Implement the layer renderer in `packages/scene-runtime/src/layers/<kind>.ts`.
- Requirements for the renderer:
  - Pure deterministic function of time `f(timeMs)`. Zero calls to `Date.now()`, `performance.now()`, or `Math.random()`.
  - Adhere to the Single Transform Owner rule: write `transform`, `opacity`, and `filter` only via `transform.ts`; set anchor (`left`, `top`) once during layer initialization.
  - Implement full In/Out animation envelopes (`envelope.ts`) for temporary effects.
- Register the renderer in `packages/scene-runtime/src/layers/index.ts` (`renderLayer` switch).

## 5. Bounds Telemetry & Inspection Integration (`packages/scene-runtime/src/scene-builder.ts`)
- Implement bounding box telemetry in `makeFrameDescriber()` in `packages/scene-runtime/src/scene-builder.ts` (published as `window.describeFrame` and `layerBoundsReport` in `packages/scene-runtime/src/index.ts`).
- Calculate accurate intrinsic `{ left, top, width, height }` bounds for `getLayerBoundsAt()` and `describeFrame()`.
- Ensure bounds can be queried with zero rasterisation via `window.seekToFrameForLayout()`.

## 6. Minimal Studio Type Compatibility (`packages/studio/`)
- Update layer union types and switch statements in `packages/studio/src/` (e.g., inspector layer panels, timeline clip renderers).
- Maintain complete type compatibility across all workspaces so `npm run typecheck -ws` passes cleanly without warnings or errors.

## 7. Unit & Contract Tests
- Add comprehensive schema validation tests in `packages/scene-spec/tests/`.
- Add runtime rendering tests in `packages/scene-runtime/tests/`.
- If an MCP tool or engine method was added, add integration tests in `packages/core-engine/tests/` and `packages/mcp-server/tests/`.

## 8. Verification & Progress Tracker Update
- Execute full static and unit verification:
  ```bash
  npm run typecheck -ws
  npm run build -ws
  npm test
  node scripts/verify-no-emoji.cjs
  ```
- Update `docs/mcp-evolution/01_PROGRESS_TRACKER.md` with the corresponding milestone status, test coverage, and verification results.
